IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-1984`
IMPORT `cat-act-facts`

-- Cat Regulations 2012 (WA), compilation 02-b0-00, currency start 24 Jul 2025 (mrdoc_48735),
-- the provisions Parts 1 and 2 of the Cat Act 2011 depend on: rr 4-19 and Schedule 3 cl 1
-- items 1-3. LQA run cat-act-2011-lqa, step 4A, 2026-10-01. Inside the run's scope (3H).
--
-- Where a regulation uses a term the Act defines ("cat management facility" in r 9(2)(d),
-- "microchip implanter" in r 8), the Act's answer is passed in as an argument: Part 1 imports
-- this module, so this module cannot import Part 1. The argument names say which term it is.
-- Reference-register entries: REF-05, 07, 09, 10, 13, 16, 18, 21-23, 27-29, 31, 33-38.

§ `r 4 -- Cat management facility operators (s. 3(1))`

-- r 4: "each of the following bodies are prescribed as operators of a facility for keeping
-- cats — (a) Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as "Cat Haven"; (b) The Royal Society for the
-- Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 4
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`r 4 -- the prescribed operators` MEANS
    LIST "Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven",
         "The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia"

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 4
GIVEN `the operator` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 4 -- is a prescribed operator` `the operator` IF
        "each of the following bodies are prescribed as operators of a facility for keeping cats"
    ... `the operator` `is among` `r 4 -- the prescribed operators`

§ `r 5 -- Microchip devices (s. 3(1))`

-- r 5(1): "an identification device must be of a type that complies with both of the following
-- Australian Standards — (a) AS 5018 — 2001 ... as amended from time to time; (b) AS 5019 —
-- 2001 ... as amended from time to time." Compliance is a fact (REF-08). r 5(2)-(3) create
-- offences that Parts 1-2 do not depend on and are not encoded (coverage.json).
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 5(1)
GIVEN i IS AN `Implant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 5(1) -- the device is of the prescribed type` i IF
        "(a) AS 5018 ... (b) AS 5019" ... i's `device complies with AS 5018-2001 and AS 5019-2001`

§ `r 6 -- Microchip database companies (s. 3(1))`

-- r 6: "(a) Central Animal Records (Aust) Pty Ltd; (ba) Global Microchip Registry Pty Ltd,
-- trading as "Global Micro Animal Registry"; [(b) deleted] (c) PetBase Pty Ltd, trading as
-- "Petsafe"; (d) Royal Agricultural Society of NSW (ABN 69 793 644 351), trading as
-- "Australasian Animal Registry". [(e) deleted]"
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 6
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`r 6 -- the prescribed microchip database companies` MEANS
    LIST "Central Animal Records (Aust) Pty Ltd",
         "Global Microchip Registry Pty Ltd, trading as Global Micro Animal Registry",
         "PetBase Pty Ltd, trading as Petsafe",
         "Royal Agricultural Society of NSW, trading as Australasian Animal Registry"

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 6
GIVEN c IS A `Database company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 6 -- is prescribed as a microchip database company` c IF
    (c's `company name`) `is among` `r 6 -- the prescribed microchip database companies`

§ `r 7 -- Microchip implanters (s. 3(1))`

-- r 7(1): "each of the following persons is prescribed — (a) a veterinarian; (b) a veterinary
-- nurse, as defined in the Veterinary Practice Act 2021 section 3."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 7(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 7(1) -- is a prescribed person` p IF
        "(a)" ... p's `is a veterinarian`
    ..  "(b)" ... p's `is a veterinary nurse`

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 7(2)(a)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`r 7(2)(a) -- the units of competency` MEANS
    LIST "ACMMIC401A", "ACMMIC401"

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 7(2)(b)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`r 7(2)(b) -- the courses` MEANS
    LIST "ACM40412", "LGAREGS404A", "LGA40504", "ACM30210", "ACMSS00001",
         "ACMSS00007", "ACM30410", "ACM40110", "ACM40210", "ACM40310"

-- r 7(2): "The qualifications ... comprise the successful completion of — (a) one or more of
-- the following units of competency ... and (b) one or more of the following courses
-- (provided by a registered training provider)". REF-12: completion with a registered
-- training provider is a fact; the lists hold only codes so completed.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 7(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 7(2) -- holds the prescribed qualifications` p IF
        "(a) one or more of the following units of competency"
    ... `r 7(2)(a) -- the units of competency` `share a name with` (p's `units of competency completed`)
    ... "and (b) one or more of the following courses"
    ... `r 7(2)(b) -- the courses` `share a name with` (p's `courses completed`)

§ `r 8 -- Microchipping cat (s. 3(1))`

-- r 8: "a microchip is implanted in the prescribed manner if it is implanted by a microchip
-- implanter." "Microchip implanter" is the Act's s 3(1) term; the caller supplies it.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 8
GIVEN `the implanter is a microchip implanter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 8 -- implanted in the prescribed manner` `the implanter is a microchip implanter` IF
        "if it is implanted by a microchip implanter" ... `the implanter is a microchip implanter`

§ `r 9 -- Cats exempt from registration (s. 5(2)(c) and 9(2)(b))`

-- r 9(2): "a cat that is in the custody of any of the following is exempt from registration —
-- (a) Cat Haven; (b) RSPCA WA; (c) the Commonwealth biosecurity Department; (d) a cat
-- management facility; (e) veterinary premises as defined in the Veterinary Practice Act 2021
-- section 3." Whether a facility is a cat management facility is the Act's question (s 3(1)).
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 9(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, `the facility is a cat management facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 9(2) -- is in the custody of a listed body` c `, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility` IF
    CONSIDER c's `in the custody of`
    WHEN `Cat Haven` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `RSPCA WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Commonwealth biosecurity Department` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a facility` f THEN `the facility is a cat management facility`
    WHEN `veterinary premises` registered THEN registered
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- r 9(3): "a cat that is in foster care is exempt from registration if — (a) the cat has been
-- placed into that foster care by either of [Cat Haven, RSPCA WA]; or (b) the cat has been
-- placed into that foster care by a SAFE entity, provided that the cat has not been in foster
-- care for more than a total of 12 weeks." 12 weeks is counted as 84 days.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 9(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 9(3) -- is in exempt foster care` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `foster care`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST fc THEN
        CONSIDER fc's `placed by`
        WHEN `Cat Haven` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `RSPCA WA` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a SAFE entity` s THEN fc's `total days the cat has been in foster care` AT MOST (12 TIMES 7)
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 9
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`, `the facility is a cat management facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 9 -- belongs to the class of cats prescribed as exempt from registration` c `, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility` IF
        "(2) in the custody of" ... `r 9(2) -- is in the custody of a listed body` c `, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility`
    ..  "(3) in foster care"     ... `r 9(3) -- is in exempt foster care` c

§ `r 10 -- Cats exempt from wearing tag (s. 6(2))`

-- r 10(1): "exhibited means exhibited for show purposes at a cat show held by — (a) Cat
-- Owners' Association of Western Australia Incorporated; or (b) the Feline Control Council of
-- Western Australia (Inc); or (c) Australian National Cats Incorporated; or (d) Cats United WA
-- Incorporated; or (e) a body that is affiliated with an organisation mentioned in (a)-(d)."
-- r 10(2): "The owner of a cat that is being exhibited is exempt from the requirement to ensure
-- the cat wears its registration tag in a public place in section 6(1) of the Act, but only
-- while that cat is being exhibited."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 10
GIVEN o IS AN `Outing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 10 -- the cat is being exhibited` o IF
    CONSIDER o's `the cat is being exhibited for show purposes at a cat show held by`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST h THEN
        CONSIDER h
        WHEN `another body` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§ `r 11 -- Application for registration (s. 8(2))`

-- r 11(1): an application "must — (a) be made by supplying the details required in Form 1
-- Parts A, B, D, F and G to the local government; and (b) be accompanied by the application
-- fee payable under Schedule 3." r 11(2)-(3) (hard copy or online; no signature online) are
-- about how the details are supplied and change no outcome here.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 11(1)(a)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 11(1)(a) -- the details of Form 1 Parts A, B, D, F and G are supplied` a IF
        `Part A` `is a part among` (a's `details supplied from Form 1`)
    AND `Part B` `is a part among` (a's `details supplied from Form 1`)
    AND `Part D` `is a part among` (a's `details supplied from Form 1`)
    AND `Part F` `is a part among` (a's `details supplied from Form 1`)
    AND `Part G` `is a part among` (a's `details supplied from Form 1`)

§ `Schedule 3 -- Fees`

-- Sch 3 Table item 1: "Fee for application for grant or renewal of the registration of a cat
-- for one year — (a) if application is for grant of registration and is made after 31 May for
-- registration until the next 31 October [$10.00] (b) otherwise [$20.00]". Item 2: 3 years
-- $42.50. Item 3: for life $100.00.
-- FORK-07: "after 31 May" read as on or after 1 June and on or before the next 31 October,
-- that is, in June to October of the same year (reading A). Reading B (any day after 31 May
-- of the application's calendar year, so June to December) is encoded beside it.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(2), Table item 1(a)
GIVEN d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Sch 3 item 1(a) -- made after 31 May for registration until the next 31 October` d IF
        "made after 31 May for registration until the next 31 October"
    ... d's `month` AT LEAST 6
    ... d's `month` AT MOST 10

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 Table item 1(a)
GIVEN d IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Sch 3 item 1(a) -- made after 31 May, reading B` d IF
    d's `month` AT LEAST 6

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(2), Table items 1-3
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 cl 1(2) -- the fee under the Table` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `period applied for`
    WHEN `one year` THEN
        IF      a's `kind of application` EQUALS `for the grant of registration`
            AND `Sch 3 item 1(a) -- made after 31 May for registration until the next 31 October` (a's `application made on`)
        THEN 10
        ELSE 20
    WHEN `3 years` THEN 42.5
    WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN 100

-- Sch 3 cl 1(3): "if the owner of a cat is a pensioner, the fee payable for an application for
-- the grant or renewal of the registration of the cat is 50% of the fee that would otherwise be
-- payable". The applicant is taken as the owner (s 8(1)). cl 1(4): a local government may
-- reduce or waive a fee.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3 cl 1(2)-(4)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 cl 1 -- the fee payable` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `fee as reduced or waived by the local government`
    WHEN JUST reduced THEN reduced
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF a's `applicant`'s `is an eligible pensioner`
        THEN `Sch 3 cl 1(2) -- the fee under the Table` a TIMES 0.5
        ELSE `Sch 3 cl 1(2) -- the fee under the Table` a

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 11(1)
GIVEN a IS AN `Application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 11(1) -- the application is made in the manner and form prescribed and accompanied by the fee` a IF
        "(a)" ... `r 11(1)(a) -- the details of Form 1 Parts A, B, D, F and G are supplied` a
    ... "(b)" ... a's `fee paid` AT LEAST `Sch 3 cl 1 -- the fee payable` a

-- s 8(2)(c): "comply with such other requirements, if any, prescribed". None is prescribed
-- (REF-23). Encoded as an explicit empty set, so a later regulation cannot pass silently.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 8(2)(c); Cat Regulations 2012 (none)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 8(2)(c) -- the other requirements prescribed` MEANS EMPTY

§ `r 12 -- Period of registration (s. 9(7))`

-- r 12(1): "Registration of a cat may be for — (a) either one year or 3 years; or (b) for the
-- life of the cat." r 12(2)(a): registration "has effect from the period specified in the
-- registration certificate until — (i) in the case of registration for one year — the next 31
-- October, unless cancelled sooner; or (ii) in the case of registration for 3 years — 31
-- October in the final year of that period, unless cancelled sooner; or (iii) in the case of
-- registration for the life of the cat — the death of the cat, unless cancelled sooner".

-- (i) FORK-05: "the next 31 October" is the first 31 October AFTER the day the registration
-- takes effect (reading A, taken): one taking effect on 31 October runs a year.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(a)(i)
GIVEN e IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`r 12(2)(a)(i) -- the next 31 October after` e MEANS
    IF e's `month` LESS THAN 10 OR (e's `month` EQUALS 10 AND e's `day` LESS THAN 31)
    THEN `the date` (e's `year`) 10 31
    ELSE `the date` (e's `year` PLUS 1) 10 31

-- FORK-05, reading B: the next 31 October on or after the day it takes effect.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(a)(i)
GIVEN e IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`r 12(2)(a)(i) -- the next 31 October, reading B` e MEANS
    IF e's `month` AT MOST 10
    THEN `the date` (e's `year`) 10 31
    ELSE `the date` (e's `year` PLUS 1) 10 31

-- (ii) FORK-06: "31 October in the final year of that period" is the 31 October that falls in
-- the last 12 months of the 3-year period beginning on the day the registration takes effect,
-- reckoned under Interpretation Act ss 5 ("year") and 62(3) (reading A, taken).
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(a)(ii); Interpretation Act 1984 ss 5, 62(3)
GIVEN e IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`r 12(2)(a)(ii) -- 31 October in the final year of the 3-year period beginning on` e MEANS
    IF s's `month` LESS THAN 10 OR (s's `month` EQUALS 10 AND s's `day` AT MOST 31)
    THEN `the date` (s's `year`) 10 31
    ELSE `the date` (s's `year` PLUS 1) 10 31
    WHERE
        s MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` (`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 2 `years beginning on` e)

-- FORK-06, reading B: 31 October of the calendar year in which the 3-year period ends.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(a)(ii)
GIVEN e IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`r 12(2)(a)(ii) -- 31 October of the calendar year the period ends, reading B` e MEANS
    `the date` ((`s 62 -- the last day of a period of` 3 `years beginning on` e)'s `year`) 10 31

-- FORK-06, reading C: the one-year rule applied three times -- the third 31 October after the
-- day the registration takes effect.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(a)(ii) (FORK-06 reading C)
GIVEN e IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A `Calendar date`
`r 12(2)(a)(ii) -- the third 31 October after, reading C` e MEANS
    `the date` ((`r 12(2)(a)(i) -- the next 31 October after` e)'s `year` PLUS 2) 10 31

-- Whether a registration has effect on day t (r 12(2)(a), with s 9(7) and s 3(1) "registered").
-- A lifetime registration runs until the death of the cat; cancellation ends any registration.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(a); Cat Act 2011 s 9(7)
GIVEN r IS A `Registration`, `the cat has died` IS A BOOLEAN, t IS A `Calendar date`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 12(2)(a) -- the registration` r `has effect, the cat having died` `the cat has died` `, on` t IF
        "has effect from the period specified in the registration certificate"
    ... `the day number of` (r's `has effect from`) AT MOST `the day number of` t
    ... "until" ... `not yet expired`
    ... "unless cancelled sooner" ... `not cancelled`
    WHERE
        `not yet expired` MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `registered for`
            WHEN `one year` THEN `the day number of` t AT MOST `the day number of` (`r 12(2)(a)(i) -- the next 31 October after` (r's `has effect from`))
            WHEN `3 years` THEN `the day number of` t AT MOST `the day number of` (`r 12(2)(a)(ii) -- 31 October in the final year of the 3-year period beginning on` (r's `has effect from`))
            WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN NOT `the cat has died`
        `not cancelled` MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `cancelled on`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST x THEN `the day number of` t LESS THAN `the day number of` x

-- r 12(2)(b): registration "may be renewed to take effect as from 1 November in any year,
-- within the preceding period of 21 days". With Interpretation Act s 61(1)(c) the 21 days do
-- not include 1 November: they run from 11 October to 31 October.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 12(2)(b); Interpretation Act 1984 s 61(1)(c)
GIVEN t IS A `Calendar date`, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 12(2)(b) -- a renewal made on` t `may take effect from 1 November` y IF
    `s 61(1)(c) -- falls within a time of` 21 `days before` (`the date` y 11 1) `, on` t

§ `r 13 -- Changes in registration`

-- r 13: "Where a cat is registered with a local government and the owner moves to another
-- local government area, the owner may notify both the former and the new local government to
-- continue that period of registration with the new local government." What follows from the
-- notice the regulation does not say (ENCODING-NOTES.md); encoded only as the permission.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 13
GIVEN `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner has moved to another local government area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 13 -- the owner may notify both local governments to continue the period` `is registered` `and` `the owner has moved to another local government area` IF
    `is registered` AND `the owner has moved to another local government area`

§ `r 14 -- Registration certificate (s. 11(1)(b))`

-- r 14: "A registration certificate issued by a local government is to be in the form of
-- Form 2." Form 2's fields, as the information it must carry.
DECLARE `Form 2 field` IS ONE OF
    `name of cat`
    `description of cat: gender, age, sterilisation status, breed if known, colour`
    `name and address of the person who registered it`
    `name of the local government`
    `registration number of cat`
    `date the registration expires`

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 14, Sch 1 Form 2
GIVETH A LIST OF `Form 2 field`
`r 14 -- the fields of Form 2` MEANS
    LIST `name of cat`,
         `description of cat: gender, age, sterilisation status, breed if known, colour`,
         `name and address of the person who registered it`,
         `name of the local government`,
         `registration number of cat`,
         `date the registration expires`

§ `r 15 -- Registration tags (s. 76(2))`

DECLARE `Tag colour` IS ONE OF
    `orange`
    `the colour designated for the year of expiry`
    `some other colour`

DECLARE `Registration tag` HAS
    `marked with registration number`                IS A STRING
    `marked with local government name and contact number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `colour`                                         IS A `Tag colour`

-- r 15(1): "A registration tag is to be — (a) marked with a registration number issued by the
-- relevant local government; and (b) marked with the name of the local government and its
-- contact number; and (c) coloured in the colour representing the year of expiry of the
-- registration to which it relates." (2) "A lifetime registration tag is to be coloured
-- orange." (3) the Minister designates the colours by Gazette notice: which colour a year
-- carries is a fact (REF-30), so (c) is satisfied by `the colour designated for the year of
-- expiry`.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 15
GIVEN tag IS A `Registration tag`, r IS A `Registration`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 15 -- the tag` tag `meets the regulation for` r IF
        "(a)" ... tag's `marked with registration number` EQUALS r's `registration number`
    ... "(b)" ... tag's `marked with local government name and contact number`
    ... "(c), (2)" ... `the right colour`
    WHERE
        `the right colour` MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `registered for`
            WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN tag's `colour` EQUALS `orange`
            OTHERWISE tag's `colour` EQUALS `the colour designated for the year of expiry`

§ `r 16 -- Information to be recorded in local government cat register (s. 12(3))`

-- r 16(a)-(m). (m) "the breed (if known), colour and gender of the cat" is three items.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 16
GIVETH A LIST OF `Information item`
`r 16 -- the information prescribed under s 12(3)` MEANS
    LIST `the cat owner's full name`,
         `the cat owner's residential address`,
         `the cat owner's postal address`,
         `the cat owner's date of birth`,
         `the cat owner's contact telephone numbers`,
         `the cat owner's email address`,
         `details of an alternative contact`,
         `the address at which the cat is normally kept`,
         `the cat's name`,
         `the cat's registration number`,
         `the cat's sterilisation status`,
         `the cat's microchip number`,
         `the cat's breed`,
         `the cat's colour`,
         `the cat's gender`

§ `r 17 -- Information to be given by microchip implanter (s. 15)`

-- r 17(a)-(m). (m) "the age, breed (if known), colour, gender and sterilisation status of the
-- cat" is five items. r 17 does not include the owner's postal address, date of birth or an
-- alternative contact, or the registration number.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 17
GIVETH A LIST OF `Information item`
`r 17 -- the information prescribed under s 15` MEANS
    LIST `the microchip barcode information or sticker`,
         `the cat's microchip number`,
         `the microchip implanter's full name`,
         `the name of the microchip implanter's company or organisation`,
         `contact details for the microchip implanter's company or organisation`,
         `the date the cat was microchipped`,
         `the cat owner's full name`,
         `the cat owner's residential address`,
         `the cat owner's contact telephone numbers`,
         `the cat owner's email address`,
         `the address at which the cat is normally kept`,
         `the cat's name`,
         `the cat's age`,
         `the cat's breed`,
         `the cat's colour`,
         `the cat's gender`,
         `the cat's sterilisation status`

-- s 15 "in the form, if any, prescribed": none is prescribed (REF-33).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 15; Cat Regulations 2012 (none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- a form is prescribed` MEANS FALSE

-- s 20 "in the form, if any, prescribed": none is prescribed (REF-37).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 20; Cat Regulations 2012 (none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20 -- a form is prescribed` MEANS FALSE

§ `r 18 -- Manner in which cat identified as sterilised (s. 19)`

DECLARE `Means of identification` IS ONE OF
    `a sterilisation certificate given under section 21`
    `a sterilisation tattoo on the cat's ear: a broken circle with a bisecting broken line`
    `a tattoo of another design`
    `some other means`

-- r 18(1): "A cat is identified as sterilised by a sterilisation certificate given in relation
-- to that cat under section 21 of the Act or a sterilisation tattoo on the cat's ear."
-- r 18(2): "A sterilisation tattoo is to consist of a broken circle with a bisecting broken line."
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 18
GIVEN m IS A `Means of identification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 18 -- is the manner prescribed` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a sterilisation certificate given under section 21` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sterilisation tattoo on the cat's ear: a broken circle with a bisecting broken line` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§ `r 19 -- Transfer of exempt cats (s. 23(3))`

-- r 19: "The provisions of section 23(1) and (2) of the Act do not apply if a cat is being
-- transferred to an organisation or person set out in regulation 9."
-- FORK-08: the SAFE entities are "set out in regulation 9" (in r 9(1)), though r 9 names them
-- only as bodies placing cats into foster care (reading A, taken). Reading B is encoded
-- beside it. A facility counts when it is a cat management facility (r 9(2)(d)), registered
-- veterinary premises when registered (r 9(2)(e)); a foster carer is not set out.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 19
GIVEN b IS A `Body`, `the facility is a cat management facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 19 -- the recipient` b `is set out in regulation 9, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility` IF
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `Cat Haven` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `RSPCA WA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Commonwealth biosecurity Department` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a facility` f THEN `the facility is a cat management facility`
    WHEN `veterinary premises` registered THEN registered
    WHEN `a SAFE entity` s THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 r 19
GIVEN b IS A `Body`, `the facility is a cat management facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `r 19 -- reading B, the recipient` b `is set out in regulation 9, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility` IF
    CONSIDER b
    WHEN `a SAFE entity` s THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `r 19 -- the recipient` b `is set out in regulation 9, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility`

§ `Classes and circumstances prescribed as none`

-- s 18(2)(c) and s 23(2)(a)(iii): "a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation".
-- No regulation prescribes one (REF-35). An explicit empty class, so the empty set is a
-- recorded decision.
@ref Cat Act 2011 ss 18(2)(c), 23(2)(a)(iii); Cat Regulations 2012 (none)
GIVEN c IS A `Cat`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no regulation -- belongs to a class of cats prescribed as exempt from sterilisation` c IF FALSE

-- s 6(2): "a class of cats prescribed as exempt from wearing registration tags when in a
-- public place". r 10 is the only regulation made for s 6(2), and it exempts the owner while
-- the cat is exhibited; no other class is prescribed.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 6(2); Cat Regulations 2012 r 10
GIVEN o IS AN `Outing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(2), r 10 -- the cat belongs to a class exempt from wearing tags in a public place` o IF
    `r 10 -- the cat is being exhibited` o

-- s 23(3): "This section, or a part of this section prescribed, does not apply — (a) in respect
-- of a cat that belongs to a class of cats, if any, prescribed; or (b) in the circumstances, if
-- any, prescribed." r 19 is the only regulation made for s 23(3): it disapplies s 23(1) and
-- (2) in the circumstance of a transfer to a body set out in r 9.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 23(3); Cat Regulations 2012 r 19
GIVEN tr IS A `Transfer`, `the facility is a cat management facility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(3), r 19 -- section 23(1) and (2) do not apply to` tr `, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility` IF
    `r 19 -- the recipient` (tr's `the recipient is`) `is set out in regulation 9, the facility being a cat management facility` `the facility is a cat management facility`
